00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:56.804
Timber Creek Financial and diversified royalty are the pair Motley Fool Canada uses to show

00:01:56.804 --> 00:02:03.144
how roughly $45,000 split between those two monthly payers can throw off about $400

00:02:03.144 --> 00:02:06.044
a month inside a TFA at current yields.

00:02:06.704 --> 00:02:11.164
Matching that cash to a bill is like lining up hydro auto pay with the day your paycheck

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:11.644
lands.

00:02:11.644 --> 00:02:15.144
The money is already there, so the bill never becomes a decision.

00:02:15.684 --> 00:02:20.524
And inside a TFSA, those distributions do not trigger a taxable event on the way in.

00:02:21.164 --> 00:02:25.044
Granite real estate investment trust is the worked example on the same screen.

00:02:25.604 --> 00:02:35.164
A $15,000 position at $86.92 per unit produces about $51.25 a month, or $615 a year.

00:02:35.164 --> 00:02:40.824
You see two names clearing a 4% monthly screen and a re-printing higher revenue beside

00:02:40.824 --> 00:02:41.184
them.

00:02:41.624 --> 00:02:46.784
Do you split the 45,000 for the 400 a month or concentrate in the industrial name?

00:02:47.484 --> 00:02:48.684
Here's how I'd think about it.

00:02:49.024 --> 00:02:55.024
Open your brokerage screener, set distribution frequency to monthly and yield above 4%, then

00:02:55.024 --> 00:02:59.424
read the latest distribution history and the payout ratio on each name before you size

00:02:59.424 --> 00:02:59.964
anything.

00:02:59.964 --> 00:03:10.824
Revenue at Granite rose $8.9% to $497.5 million, and net operating income rose $7.8% to $405.7 million

00:03:10.824 --> 00:03:17.324
for the nine months ended September 30th, 2026, which is the fundamental check after the yield

00:03:17.324 --> 00:03:23.484
filter, not a substitute for it. Always confirm the distribution is classified as return of capital

00:03:23.484 --> 00:03:29.384
or eligible dividend before purchase, so you do not get a surprise tax slip inside the TFSA.

00:03:29.964 --> 00:03:33.464
and treat the whole method as income that has worked in lower rate stretches

00:03:33.464 --> 00:03:36.884
and loses ground when central banks signal faster hikes.

00:03:37.829 --> 00:03:40.209
Open your TFSA holdings list this week.

00:03:40.729 --> 00:03:44.889
Identify any monthly payer trading within 5% of its 50-session average

00:03:45.269 --> 00:03:48.609
and write down its current yield and most recent distribution amount

00:03:48.609 --> 00:03:50.909
so the screen is a habit, not a headline.

00:03:51.689 --> 00:03:55.649
Granite real estate investment trust, the monthly payer we just screened

00:03:55.649 --> 00:03:58.149
stays a watch rather than a simulated fill

00:03:58.149 --> 00:04:02.669
bill, and this is a simulated trade for learning purposes with no real money attached.

